  "rules": [
    "A phase 2 case is checked by the checker its inventory row names, with the adapted verifiers of som-rs/behavior/phase2/adapted (adapt.py) and the phase2_host language steps.",
    "The Rust reference is the checker's oracle. A Rust product passes a case when its checker passes and no assembled file changed during the run.",
    "A Python product that fails its own oracle is a python_defect: Rust is still checked against the oracle and the Python output stays byte-identical.",
    "A case the phase 2 profile refuses is not a behavior case for Rust; Rust refuses its prompt.",
    "Not-applicable records are counted from the outcomes of the Python run; a Rust run must record the same cases as not applicable."
  ],
